@exam final-exam | Final Assessment
? mcq: Which keyword declares a compile-time constant in Dart?
- final
+ const
- var
- late
> const values are fixed at compile time.
? tf: In Dart 3, a variable of type String can hold null.
= false
> Only String? can hold null.
? mcq: What does the ?? operator do?
+ Returns the right side when the left side is null
- Throws if the value is null
- Compares two values
- Declares a nullable type
> ?? supplies a fallback for null.
? output: What does this print?
```dart
void main() {
  print([1, 2, 3].map((n) => n * 2).toList());
}
```
+ [2, 4, 6]
- [1, 2, 3]
- 12
- [2, 3, 4]
> map doubles each element.
? mcq: Which construct makes switches over a closed set of subtypes exhaustive?
- abstract class
+ sealed class
- mixin
- typedef
> Sealed hierarchies are checked for exhaustiveness.
? fill: An async function that returns an int has the return type Future<___>.
= int
> async functions wrap results in a Future.
? mcq: What is the best tool for CPU-heavy work that would freeze the UI?
+ An isolate (Isolate.run or compute)
- More await keywords
- A Timer
- setState
> Isolates run work in parallel without blocking the UI isolate.
? mcq: Which widget arranges children vertically?
- Row
+ Column
- Stack
- Wrap
> Column lays out vertically.
? tf: setState should be called inside build to refresh the UI.
= false
> Calling setState during build causes errors.
? mcq: Where should you dispose a TextEditingController?
+ In State.dispose()
- In build()
- In initState()
- Never
> Controllers must be disposed.
? mcq: What does Expanded do inside a Row?
+ Makes the child fill the remaining horizontal space
- Centres the child
- Adds padding
- Makes the row scroll
> Expanded fills the remaining main-axis space.
? mcq: Which list constructor builds items lazily?
- ListView(children: ...)
+ ListView.builder
- Column
- Wrap
> builder creates only visible items.
? fill: To read the screen width efficiently, call MediaQuery.___(context).width.
= sizeOf
> sizeOf only rebuilds when the size changes.
? mcq: Which package is the Flutter team's recommended router?
+ go_router
- http
- provider
- sqflite
> go_router supports declarative, URL-based routing.
? mcq: In Provider, which call should be used inside button callbacks?
- context.watch
+ context.read
- context.listen
- context.build
> read gets the object without subscribing to changes.
? tf: Secrets such as auth tokens should be stored in SharedPreferences.
= false
> Use secure storage for secrets.
? mcq: Which HTTP status code range indicates server errors?
- 2xx
- 3xx
- 4xx
+ 5xx
> 5xx codes are server errors.
? scenario: A screen shows stale search results from an older query. What is the best fix?
+ Ignore responses that don't match the latest query
- Increase the timeout
- Remove async code
- Use a const widget
> Discard stale responses.
? mcq: Which file format must you upload to Google Play?
- .apk only
+ .aab (Android App Bundle)
- .ipa
- .zip
> Play requires App Bundles for new apps.
? mcq: Which widget test function finds widgets by text?
+ find.text
- find.widget
- search.text
- expect.text
> find.text locates Text widgets.
? tf: Hot reload preserves the current app state.
= true
> Hot reload keeps state; hot restart resets it.
? mcq: What decides whether Flutter reuses an element when rebuilding?
+ The widget's runtimeType and key
- The widget's colour
- The build method's length
- The number of children only
> Widget.canUpdate compares type and key.
? mcq: Which Firebase feature enforces who can read and write data?
- Analytics
+ Security rules
- Crashlytics
- Remote Config
> Rules run on the server and enforce access.
? fill: The keyword used to emit values from an async* function is ___.
= yield
> yield adds values to the stream.
? mcq: How should you roll out a risky release on Google Play?
+ A staged rollout to a percentage of users
- Release to 100% immediately
- Skip testing tracks
- Upload an APK by email
> Staged rollouts limit the impact of problems.
